load @term/seed/group
  find group

# The general linear group: the group of all invertible linear maps of a vector space, equivalently the invertible
# square matrices, under composition. It is the largest matrix group, and every other classical group (orthogonal,
# unitary, symplectic) is a subgroup cut out by a preserved structure. The determinant is a homomorphism from it to the
# nonzero scalars. The form carries the underlying group; invertibility is the defining condition.
form general-linear-group
  link group, like group
